## The data

A university wants to flag students likely to fail their final exam while there is still
time to help. Twenty historical records describe four habits and the result:

<table class="hz-table"><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Attendance</th><th>Study Hours</th><th>Assignment</th><th>Previous Grade</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>S01</td><td>High</td><td>High</td><td>Yes</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S02</td><td>High</td><td>Medium</td><td>Yes</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S03</td><td>Low</td><td>Low</td><td>No</td><td>Poor</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>S04</td><td>Medium</td><td>High</td><td>Yes</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S05</td><td>Low</td><td>Medium</td><td>No</td><td>Poor</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>S06</td><td>High</td><td>Low</td><td>Yes</td><td>Poor</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S07</td><td>Medium</td><td>Medium</td><td>Yes</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S08</td><td>Low</td><td>High</td><td>Yes</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S09</td><td>Medium</td><td>Low</td><td>No</td><td>Poor</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>S10</td><td>High</td><td>High</td><td>No</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S11</td><td>Low</td><td>Low</td><td>Yes</td><td>Poor</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>S12</td><td>Medium</td><td>High</td><td>No</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S13</td><td>High</td><td>Medium</td><td>No</td><td>Poor</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>S14</td><td>Medium</td><td>Medium</td><td>No</td><td>Poor</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>S15</td><td>Low</td><td>Medium</td><td>Yes</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S16</td><td>High</td><td>Low</td><td>No</td><td>Poor</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>S17</td><td>Medium</td><td>Low</td><td>Yes</td><td>Good</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S18</td><td>Low</td><td>High</td><td>No</td><td>Poor</td><td>Fail</td></tr><tr><td>S19</td><td>High</td><td>High</td><td>Yes</td><td>Poor</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>S20</td><td>Medium</td><td>High</td><td>Yes</td><td>Poor</td><td>Pass</td></tr></tbody></table>



With 12 passes and 8 fails, the starting entropy is

$$H(S) = -\left[0.6\log_2 0.6 + 0.4\log_2 0.4\right] = 0.9710 \text{ bits},$$

close to the 1-bit maximum: knowing nothing else, we are very unsure about any student.



## Choosing the root: hand versus code

ID3 picks the attribute whose split removes the most uncertainty,
$IG(S, A) = H(S) - \sum_v \frac{|S_v|}{|S|} H(S_v)$. The values in the report were
derived by hand with five-decimal logarithms; the code recomputes them exactly.

